          %p
            where the right vertical functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgets
            the phase assignments and just remembers the correspondences of field trajectories.
          %p
            So far this is a non-local (or: not-necessarily local) prequantum field theory, since it assigns data only to entire
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifolds"} closed manifolds
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+quantum+field+theory"} local quantum field theory
          %p
            In order to formalize this localization, we allow the cobordisms to contain higher-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            pieces that are
            = succeed "." do
