          #FreeLoopSpaceOfGroupoid.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+space+object"} free loop space object
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi X
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi Π
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [\Pi(S^1), X]
                    \\simeq
                    X \underset{[\Pi(S^0), X]}{\times}X
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Notice that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(S^0) \simeq \ast \coprod \ast
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space+object"} path space object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo •
                      %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Pi(S^0), X_\bullet]^I_\bullet
              has
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  objects are pairs of morphisms in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mo •
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
              %li
                %p morphisms are commuting squares of such.
            %p
              Now the fiber product in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyFiberProductOfGroupoids"}
              picks in there those pairs of morphisms for which both start at the same object, and both end at the same object. Therefore
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi Π
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo •
                      %mi I
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi Π
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo •
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \underset{[\Pi(S^0), X_\bullet]_\bullet}{\times} [\Pi(S^0), X_\bullet]^I_\bullet \underset{[\Pi(S^0), X_\bullet]_\bullet}{\times} X
              is the groupoid whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  objects are diagrams in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
                  of the form
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
