                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \underset{[\Pi_1(S^1), X]}{\times} X
                    \\simeq [\Pi_1(S^1), X]
                    \\,.
            %p
              Along these lines one checks the required
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zag+identities"} zig-zag identities
          %h5#1dDWLocalFieldTheory Action functionals on spaces of trajectories: correspondences of groupoids over the space of phases
          %p
            We have now assembled all the ingredients need in order to formally regard a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+character"} group character
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \colon G \to U(1)
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            as a local action functional of a prequantum field theory, hence as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+dualizable+object"} fully dualizable object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
