          #1dPathIntegralViaSchur.num_remark
            %h6#remark_12 Remark
            %p
              It follows that in a discussion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
              of 1d DW theory is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schur+inner+product"} Schur integral
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+character"} group character
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
