                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\frac{1}{\vert G \vert}
                    \\underset{g\in G}{\sum}
                    c(g)
                    \=
                    \\langle c,1\rangle
                    \\,.
          %p
            In conclusion,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-dimensional+Dijkgraaf-Witten+theory"} 1-dimensional Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
            as a prequantum field theory comes down to be essentially a geometric interpretation of what
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+characters"} group characters
            are and do. One may regard this as a simple example of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+representation+theory"} geometric representation theory
          %h4#2d_dijkgraafwitten_theory 2d Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
          %p
