                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{B}G_{conn} \to \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)_{conn}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+n-bundle"} prequantum 3-bundle
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+circle+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons circle 3-bundle
          %p
            Many more examples… e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 7d Chern-Simons theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AKSZ+sigma-model"} AKSZ sigma-model
          %h5#geometric_defects_for__from_chernsimons_invariants_higher_holonomy_parallel_transport_fiber_integration_in_differential_cohomology
            Geometric defects for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi tYM
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{tYM}
            from Chern-Simons invariants: Higher holonomy, parallel transport, fiber integration in differential cohomology
          %p
            While we may think of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category+of+cobordisms"} (∞,n)-category of cobordisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bord_n
            as built from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+theorem"} cobordism theorem
            clearly states that these just serve as a presentation of a structure that is not intrinsically related to smooth or even topological structure. This is made manifest by prop.
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ValueOfLocalPrequantumFieldTheoryOnCobordism"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-morphism"} k-morphism
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bord_n
            depends only on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of the
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-morphism." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field+theory"} topological field theory
            is referring to.
          %p
            But boundaries and defects of a topological field theory may add extra structure to the theory which is not “purely topological” in this way. Here we consider a canonical class of defects for universal higher topological Yang-Mills theory, def.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralHighertYM"}
            = succeed "-Chern-Simons" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HigherCSAsBoundaryTheory"}
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+parallel+transport"} higher parallel transport
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+holonomy"} higher holonomy
            of the higher Chern-Simons type action functionals over actual
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
          #FiberIntegrationInDiffCohomologyAsDiagram.num_prop
