          %h2#references References
          %p For introduction and survey see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+Prequantum+Geometry"} Higher Prequantum Geometry
          %p
            The idea of formulating local prequantum field theory by spans in a slice over a “space of phases” in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            has been expressed in the unpublished note
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Nonabelian+cocycles+and+their+quantum+symmetries"} Nonabelian cocycles and their quantum symmetries
              (2008)
          %p
            A formulation of the idea for
            = succeed "-type" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dijkgraaf-Witten+theory"} Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
          %ul
            %li#FHLT
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"} Jacob Lurie
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topological+Quantum+Field+Theories+from+Compact+Lie+Groups"} Topological Quantum Field Theories from Compact Lie Groups
              (2010)
          %p based on the considerations in section 3.2 of
          %ul
            %li#LurieTFT
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/On+the+Classification+of+Topological+Field+Theories"} On the Classification of Topological Field Theories
              (2009).
          %p
            Based on the general formulation of the more general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QFT+with+defects"} field theory with defects
            described in section 4.3 there, in
          %ul#FiorenzaValentino
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessandro+Valentino"} Alessandro Valentino
              %em Boundary conditions in local TFTs
              (in preparation)
          %p
            the structure of such
            = succeed "/defects/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+walls"} domain walls
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            are analyzed in the prequantum theory, hence with coefficients in an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category+of+spans"} (∞,n)-category of spans
          %p
            The study of local prequantum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            with its codimension-1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Wess-Zumino-Witten+theory"} ∞-Wess-Zumino-Witten theory
            and codimension 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+line"}> Wilson line
            \-theory in this fashion, in an ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            is discussed in
          %ul#hCSlpQFT
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              et al.,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Local+prequantum+field+theory"} Local prequantum field theory
          %p Much of the content of this entry here serve as, or arose as, lecture notes for
          %ul#SchreiberPittLectures
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+Chern-Simons+theory+Introduction"} Higher Chern-Simons theory Introduction
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://www.pitt.edu/~jdeblois/CS.html"} Chern-Simons Theory: Geometry, Topology and Physics
              University of Pittsburgh (May 2013)
          %p
            Later this was developed further with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Khavkine"} Igor Khavkine
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://www.physicsforums.com/insights/higher-prequantum-geometry-need-prequantum-geometry/"} Higher prequantum geometry I: The need for prequantum geometry
            %li
